00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.150 align:start position:0%
 
a show of support in a time of war  the u.s secretaries of state and defense  in the ukrainian capital to meet  president vladimir zelinsky  this was the first high-level visit by  u.s officials since russian forces  invaded  what you've done  in repelling the russians in the battle  of kiev is was extraordinary  and uh and inspiring quite frankly to  the rest of the world we've gotten used  to seeing you on video  around the world but it's great it's  good to see you in person  during a three-hour meeting the pair  promised to step up u.s military aid  including sending more advanced weapons  we will continue to do everything  possible to ensure that you're  successful  ukraine's president has accused allies  of being too slow to help saying they  shared responsibility for the war's  casualties but on sunday he said he was  grateful for u.s support and what he  called an important moment for his  country  the priority of this meeting is weaponry  support from the united states and our  partners in europe it's all about the  strength of our army and the second  issue is the sanctions against the  russian federation because of the  full-scale terror the russians are  waging in our country  while russia has failed to capture any  major city since the invasion started on  february 24th it has caused widespread  devastation  cities in the east and south are facing  daily bombardment what president  vladimir zelinski's called the battle  for donbass  the u.s says it wants to see russia  weakened so that it can never do  anything like this again  the bottom line  is this  we don't know how  the rest of this war will unfold  but we do know  that a sovereign independent ukraine  will be around a lot longer than  vladimir putin's on the scene  in terms of russia's war aims russia has  already failed and ukraine has already  succeeded  speaking in poland after their meeting  the secretaries outlined what will be  included in the latest 700 million  dollar package to ukraine and  neighbouring countries  so they need long-range fires  you've heard them express a need for  tanks we believe that they we can win  they can win if they have the right  equipment the right support the visit  comes just days before the u.n secretary  general antonio gutierrez is due to  travel to moscow then keefe for meetings  with leaders from both sides secretary  blinken says guterres will be carrying a  strong and clear message to the russian  president but he needs to end this war  now  alexia bryan al-jazeera  live to my kana in washington dc mike a  strong message of solidarity from the  biden administration there and the u.s  resuming its diplomatic presence in  ukraine  yes uh very strong developments in terms  of u.s support for ukraine its most  senior cabinet officials being sent  there and the secretary of state and the  secretary of defense meeting there with  ukrainian president vladimir zelinsky  certainly this is a strong signal from  the united states and one must note too  that it has now announced a new  ambassador to ukraine  bridget brink is the current ambassador  to slovakia  she is a professional diplomat this is  very important and also she is extremely  experienced within the region and she  would be well known by the us's european  allies which would be of great comfort  to them having a diplomat in place who  they are well aware of and who they know  and who is not a political appointment  who is a career state department officer  so all of these factors together very  important in terms of the us  presence in ukraine saying as well that  it's sending diplomats back in the  coming week those diplomats having been  brought out at the beginning of the war  and also significantly the us is going  to resume training of ukrainian military  on what it says are undisclosed weapon  systems so all of these factors together  show an uptick in the biden  administration's involvement in that war  in ukraine  mike hanna in washington dc thank you  very much for that let's go now live to  charlie stratford  who joins us from the front line in  eastern ukraine you're near the city of  slovyansk which is close to the front  line i understand tell us about what's  been happening  yeah we're not actually on the front  line here but then front lines seem to  be moving so  rapidly some days in this area of  eastern ukraine we're actually north of  slovansk which is one of the biggest  cities that is still under full  ukrainian government military control  adjacent to the city of krematorsk as  well a very large urban area the road  behind me leads up to a town called  isiam  which  the russian military have controlled for  a number of weeks they are trying to  push down this road to basically  surround slavyans which is to say is in  that direction earlier today  this morning we were close to a town  called liman which is to my left which  is to the east of here um and we know  there's a lot of heavy fighting going on  in that town we were speaking to  civilians that were being evacuated out  of it volunteers ukrainian volunteers  going in and picking them up them  describing  terrifying scenes as as we've been  reporting for weeks now as these  civilians try and evacuate areas  as seemingly the russians make a push  towards slavyansk we also saw ambulances  coming out uh we saw one wounded  ukrainian soldiers obviously the  ukrainian military very sensitive about  showing that sort of information despite  obviously admitting that it is a war but  obviously concerned about the identities  of injured uh military personnel  we also understand that there is a push  to the west of here also towards  slavians we understand that the russian  military are hitting targets there in  the last few minutes from where i'm  standing we've seen missiles being  launched  towards what can only be described or we  understand would be targets in the east  russian positions  from in front of me and just just to the  left here as well  we had a lot of incoming and outgoing  shelling early in the morning the thing  situation has calmed down  in the last couple of hours in this area  but as i say the ukrainian military are  claiming that  russian forces trying to push towards  serbians have so far failed in that  endeavor  but this is one could only really  describe it potentially as being the  quiet before the storm the streets of  slavyansk are pretty much empty  we i can still hear a siren being an  alarm  in the distance  most of the civilians of slovenians have  have left  and the reason why this area is so  important as i say is because it is one  of the largest urban areas still under  ukrainian control  russian forces pushing in from from the  northeast  the north and the northwest as well as  certain areas of the east  the ukrainian military is saying that  there is ongoing fighting in various  villages to the east of here also with  respect to what's going on in mariopol  of course that city that has seen such  heavy fighting as according to some  reports and we've seen the pictures as  as the world has a city that has pretty  much been flattened um the ukrainian  deputy prime minister saying there is as  yet still no agreement the russians are  still she's saying the russians still  refusing to agree on setting up some  sort of humanitarian corridor to get out  what we understand are around a thousand  civilians trapped  under that steel works that giant great  soviet-built industrial plant where um  still there are ukrainian fighters  ukrainian military in there we  understand that uh obviously the  civilians haven't left um and there is  still fighting to try as the russians  try and clear that area of those  ukrainian fighters and ukrainian  military so of course great concern  they're still for those civilians  trapped um in mariopol but as i say  there are still a lot of civilians  trapped in towns around this area as it  seems the russians russian military  forces try and push  towards slavyansk all right charlie  thank you very much for that update  charles stratford in slovak there now to  moscow where russian president vladimir  putin has been speaking in the last few  hours he was addressing a meeting of the  general prosecutor's office let's bring  in dorset jabari in moscow forest the  president we heard  a very defiant message from vladimir  putin  yes certainly  the russian president was  discussing the  upcoming year and the agenda and the  main issues that his country's general  prosecutor's office will have to focus  on according to vladimir putin the  members of this office have to remain  vigilant and united because he believes  that there is a full scale campaign  being waged against  his country's  media as well as the  military  the president's saying that  there is a lot of misinformation and  provocations against the russia's the  russian military so it is the job of the  general prosecutor's office to  prevent the spread of fake information  uh online and from for media vladimir  putin seemingly very directly  targeting the foreign media saying that  they are extremists that are being their  views being presented in the foreign  media and he advised his  general prosecutor's office to remain  vigilant he also shared some information  about a  operation that the  fsb uh managed to prevent from taking  place according to the president the  federal security services thwarted an  attempt on the life of a very prominent  state tv presenter vladimir sullivan who  is one of the most well-known figures in  this country he has a daily  program here in the evenings on state tv  and he is known to be very much a strong  supporter of vladimir putin and  according to the president there was a  number of arrests made by the security  services who were part of a neo-nazi  group as they called them and they have  been detained with the intention of  trying to  kill this  state tv presenter this was another  example by  vladimir putin of how  his country has been under attack from  the west and specifically the united  states he says he believes that the cia  had a hand in this as well he also  talked about the other  various forms of  the  sabotage attempts by western countries  on russian society let's listen to some  of what he had to say  the other task is coming forward to  break russia from within but they can't  do it because our society is showing its  unity and support our armed forces and  our efforts to maintain the security of  russia and the citizens of donbass  all right dorsa we heard from charlie  just a moment ago about the situation in  mario paul and those humanitarian  portals the ukrainians saying that  there's still  no humanitarian corridors open in  mariopol what is russia saying about  this  well the russian defense ministry has  been announcing these so-called  ceasefires short-term  as they are in mariopol to allow the  civilians to um evacuate that steel  plant and also allow give an opportunity  to those  ukrainian fighters that are holed up in  there to surrender this is something  that has been ongoing for the past 10  days or so but every opportunity that is  announced by the russians  seemingly does not work out the  ukrainian side accusing russia that  they're not actually  establishing any kind of ceasefire that  the attacks continue during that time  also there have been accusations that  the  civilians allowed to leave any areas  during these ceasefires are forced to go  into areas in russia and that is  something of course that the civilians  would not agree to in general but the  russian defense ministry saying that  they have on a regular basis provided  these ceasefires and it is the ukrainian  side that is not uh withholding uh  upholding rather their end of the deal  they don't want to actually evacuate the  civilians they're being used by the  ukrainian fighters that are still in  there in an attempt to prevent the  russians from storming this facility of  course the russian president had ordered  on thursday that no russian troops enter  this facility and just to seal it up and  not allow anybody to go in or out in an  attempt to basically force  whatever  fighters are left in there to surrender  at any point there is a  strong sense that this is now yet  another attempt by the russian defense  ministry to show the international  community that they are trying to  establish humanitarian corridors of  course we have the secretary general of  the united nations coming to moscow on  tuesday and certainly this will be an  example of how the russians will show  that they are trying to establish some  kind of a  ceasefire to allow those  civilians to leave but we'll have to  wait and see what the secretary general  will have to say indeed we will follow  that visit with you of course social  barrie live for us there in moscow  and the international criminal chief  prosecutor has announced that it will  participate in a joint eu investigation  team that is looking into allegations of  international crimes in ukraine

